Usage: getopt <optstring> <parameters>

Parse command options.
The enhanced getopt(1) normalizes its parameter list and prints a shell-compatible argument list.
Supports short options, long options, required ':' arguments, and optional '::' arguments.

OPTIONS:
  -o, --options ARG      short option specification
  -l, --longoptions ARG  long options to be recognized
  -n, --name ARG         name used in diagnostics
  -q, --quiet            disable error reporting by getopt
  -Q, --quiet-output     no normal output
  -s, --shell ARG        set quoting conventions to those of <shell>
  -T, --test             test for getopt(1) version
  -u, --unquoted         do not quote the output
  -a, --alternative      allow long options starting with single -
      --help             display this help and exit
  -V, --version          output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
